WEBVTT

00:01.270 --> 00:03.540
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

00:06.650 --> 00:08.540
I adjusted the transfer circle

00:08.540 --> 00:12.610
so that you can only travel between
here and the Clearflow Lake stratum.

00:12.610 --> 00:15.730
Don't worry, I set it so 
monsters can't use it.

00:15.730 --> 00:17.470
Good work, Hulemy.

00:17.470 --> 00:18.360
Well done.

00:18.360 --> 00:22.690
Oh, look at all the hard work.
I'm impressed.

00:22.690 --> 00:26.630
Once things settle down here, we might as 
well go back to the Clearflow Lake stratum.

00:26.630 --> 00:29.050
We're done patrolling.

00:28.450 --> 00:31.440
Looks like there are no 
remnants in the village.

00:31.440 --> 00:33.000
I'm so tired.

00:33.000 --> 00:36.180
Captain! Why am I paired 
up with this pervert?!

00:36.480 --> 00:40.320
Good grief, I haven't 
used any illusion magic.

00:40.320 --> 00:42.890
Where is this pervert of whom you speak?

00:42.890 --> 00:45.810
Because somebody has to stand watch.

00:45.810 --> 00:47.390
Bear with it.

00:47.390 --> 00:49.590
Oh, pay it no mind.

00:49.590 --> 00:53.140
It's a gentleman's job 
to protect a frail lady.

00:55.080 --> 00:56.710
C-Calm down, Shui.

00:56.710 --> 00:58.020
How can I be calm?!

00:58.020 --> 01:00.580
He keeps digging shoes 
out of collapsed houses,

01:00.580 --> 01:02.740
and his nose twitches as 
he tries to smell them!

01:02.740 --> 01:04.320
It's utterly gross!

01:04.320 --> 01:07.780
She seems to be emotionally 
unstable, the poor thing.

01:07.780 --> 01:09.030
Smell this!

01:11.600 --> 01:16.600
<i>This is high-level combat, but the 
reason they're fighting is tragic.</i>

01:16.600 --> 01:19.340
Hey, Boxxo. You got some time after this?

01:19.340 --> 01:20.470
<i>Y-ea.</i>

01:20.470 --> 01:21.730
That's good.

01:21.730 --> 01:25.480
I thought I'd have you stop by 
the Menagerie of Fools' base.

01:25.480 --> 01:27.480
<i>E? H-ere?</i>

01:27.480 --> 01:30.670
Yeah, it's in the Origin stratum.

01:33.110 --> 01:35.990
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine, I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:38.440 --> 01:40.300
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

01:40.300 --> 01:42.280
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

01:42.280 --> 01:47.620
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

01:43.370 --> 01:49.250
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine, I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:47.620 --> 01:50.130
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

01:50.130 --> 01:51.860
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

03:06.080 --> 03:09.960
<b>Sweet Temptation</b>

03:06.440 --> 03:11.700
<i>I'm surprised that the Menagerie of Fools 
has its base in the Origin stratum.</i>

03:11.700 --> 03:14.260
Boxxo, Lammis, Hulemy.

03:14.260 --> 03:17.720
There's something that it's 
about time we told you.

03:18.510 --> 03:23.430
Yes. It would be... best if they knew.

03:23.760 --> 03:27.140
<i>Did a shadow just cross Filmina's face?</i>

03:27.860 --> 03:30.620
<i>I think the mood's shifted for 
the red/white twins, too.</i>

03:30.620 --> 03:32.010
<i>Is something going on?</i>

03:32.010 --> 03:35.030
That's enough messing around, you two!

03:35.030 --> 03:36.820
Just give me a minute!

03:36.820 --> 03:39.270
I think I can put one 
right through his head.

03:39.270 --> 03:42.940
My, my. I haven't used any 
mental manipulation magic,

03:42.940 --> 03:45.010
and yet I'm hearing things.

03:45.320 --> 03:47.050
Sorry, Boxxo.

03:47.050 --> 03:49.020
We'll wait for those fools to settle down,

03:49.020 --> 03:51.280
and then you can all come to our base.

03:51.280 --> 03:52.730
<i>Hello there.</i>

03:54.220 --> 03:59.050
It's news to me that the Menagerie of 
Fools' base is in the Origin stratum.

03:59.050 --> 04:01.430
We didn't want it to stand out.

04:01.430 --> 04:05.010
How long have you been a member, Shui?

04:05.010 --> 04:07.150
Less than two years, still.

04:07.150 --> 04:10.680
Does that mean Hevee has been in it longer?

04:10.680 --> 04:12.940
Yes, I am her senior.

04:12.940 --> 04:18.940
But then, we do not bother with troublesome 
vertical hierarchy in the Menagerie.

04:18.940 --> 04:24.190
If we did, I would have to show respect 
to Aka and Shiro for being my seniors.

04:24.190 --> 04:27.440
That's a surprise. Aren't 
those twins younger than you?

04:27.440 --> 04:29.140
Yes, Hulemy.

04:29.140 --> 04:32.310
They are, but the first members 
of the Menagerie of Fools

04:32.310 --> 04:36.400
were Captain Kerioyl, Vice Captain 
Filmina, Aka, and Shiro.

04:36.400 --> 04:37.960
Those four.

04:37.960 --> 04:41.220
Oh yeah? I didn't know that.

04:41.220 --> 04:43.210
<i>It's the first time Shui's heard it, too?</i>

04:43.210 --> 04:46.590
Come to think of it, those four 
often disappear all at once,

04:46.590 --> 04:48.510
and they work together a lot.

04:48.770 --> 04:52.220
If you're curious, why not 
ask them about it later?

04:52.220 --> 04:54.010
<i>Wa-t-s u-p?</i>

04:54.010 --> 04:56.400
Oh, sorry, Master Boxxo.

04:56.640 --> 05:01.270
Hearing all that reminded me of 
something I've been wondering about.

05:01.270 --> 05:02.390
<i>Y-ea.</i>

05:02.390 --> 05:05.690
It's something I sense about 
Aka's and Shiro's presence...

05:05.690 --> 05:07.690
No, never mind.

05:07.690 --> 05:10.270
I shouldn't go around speculating 
about these things.

05:10.640 --> 05:13.770
<i>After hearing only that much, 
now I'm <i>really</i> curious.</i>

05:16.360 --> 05:18.120
Um...

05:18.360 --> 05:21.200
This is the menagerie's base.

05:21.200 --> 05:23.820
It sure has nice ventilation.

05:23.820 --> 05:25.580
Oh, that's not it.

05:26.280 --> 05:29.080
It's beyond this hidden door.

05:32.080 --> 05:34.340
Come on down, everyone.

05:35.840 --> 05:36.600
Hey.

05:36.600 --> 05:38.610
Sit wherever you like.

05:38.610 --> 05:42.590
Boxxo, would you mind dispensing 
drinks for everyone?

05:42.590 --> 05:43.990
<i>Hello there.</i>

05:44.230 --> 05:45.740
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

05:44.830 --> 05:48.160
Welcome to the Menagerie of Fools' hideout.

05:48.530 --> 05:51.110
We've gathered you here 
today for one reason.

05:51.110 --> 05:54.060
We figured we'd tell you our objective.

05:55.620 --> 05:57.510
First, a quick review.

05:57.510 --> 06:02.250
Do you remember how you can have a wish 
granted if you master this dungeon?

06:02.250 --> 06:07.530
"I shall grant thee a single wish 
for reaching the lowest stratum.

06:07.530 --> 06:11.650
Offer the proof that thou hast 
subdued a mighty stratum lord."

06:11.650 --> 06:13.750
I believe that's how the legend goes.

06:14.020 --> 06:17.840
Yeah, and there was a team that 
actually reached the bottom stratum

06:17.840 --> 06:19.800
of a dungeon in a land to the southwest.

06:19.800 --> 06:23.170
I hear they actually had 
their wishes granted,

06:23.770 --> 06:26.770
and that's apparently when 
the dungeon ceased to exist.

06:26.770 --> 06:28.160
<i>Huh? That means...</i>

06:28.160 --> 06:32.840
If somebody gets a wish granted, the 
Clearflow Lake stratum will be gone?!

06:32.840 --> 06:34.530
Yeah, that's right.

06:34.530 --> 06:38.540
What happens to the people inside 
a dungeon when it goes away?

06:38.540 --> 06:42.110
Seems they get forcefully 
ejected outside it.

06:42.110 --> 06:46.300
Don't worry, nobody ends up getting 
destroyed along with the dungeon.

06:47.790 --> 06:50.760
<i>Good, the residents won't 
get caught up in it.</i>

06:50.760 --> 06:51.870
So, yeah.

06:52.880 --> 06:56.630
The vice captain and I thought 
we'd reveal our wish.

06:56.630 --> 06:59.560
Sorry to keep it from you for so long.

07:04.300 --> 07:08.190
What?! There's a door there?!

07:08.190 --> 07:09.450
Come this way.

07:14.820 --> 07:15.820
Huh?

07:15.820 --> 07:17.580
What's that?

07:18.020 --> 07:20.600
<i>What in the world?</i>

07:23.000 --> 07:25.210
It's faint, but I sense a presence.

07:25.680 --> 07:27.450
He must not be dead.

07:32.650 --> 07:37.090
This... is Filmina's and my child.

07:38.690 --> 07:40.670
<i>Huh? What'd he say?</i>

07:40.670 --> 07:43.620
This boy is our son.

07:43.620 --> 07:46.140
<i>Um, I can't keep up.</i>

07:46.710 --> 07:49.390
<i>Huh? Why isn't anyone having 
much of a reaction?</i>

07:49.390 --> 07:52.090
<i>I thought there'd be 
shouts of surprise here.</i>

07:52.610 --> 07:53.750
What?!

07:53.750 --> 07:55.250
You two are married?!

07:55.250 --> 07:57.730
<i>That's what I was waiting for, Lammis!</i>

07:57.730 --> 08:00.300
<i>I did think they were quarrelsome yet close,</i>

08:00.300 --> 08:02.740
<i>but I had no idea they were 
married with a child.</i>

08:03.150 --> 08:06.010
<i>What's more, their child 
is asleep inside a crystal.</i>

08:06.010 --> 08:08.750
<i>It'd be much more unnatural 
not to be surprised.</i>

08:08.750 --> 08:10.810
Sorry to keep it a secret.

08:10.810 --> 08:13.620
It's been nearly twenty 
years since we got married.

08:13.620 --> 08:15.750
That it has, dear.

08:16.140 --> 08:19.520
And so, Aka and Shiro are our kids, too.

08:19.520 --> 08:20.640
Ehhhh?!

08:21.070 --> 08:23.170
I'm surprised you never caught on.

08:23.170 --> 08:24.390
Sorry to keep it quiet.

08:27.150 --> 08:30.540
Now it makes sense that 
Aka and Shiro's presence

08:30.540 --> 08:32.770
seemed similar to the captain's 
and vice captain's.

08:32.770 --> 08:34.990
You're not surprised, Hevee?

08:34.990 --> 08:39.770
I've never seen you lose your cool,
and I was kind of looking forward to it.

08:39.770 --> 08:42.430
Sorry to betray your expectations.

08:42.430 --> 08:45.290
I had vaguely picked up on it already.

08:45.290 --> 08:47.790
You really are crafty.

08:47.790 --> 08:51.820
Oh, so that means you two are 
that boy's big brothers?

08:51.820 --> 08:52.420
Nope.

08:52.690 --> 08:53.950
He's the oldest.

08:53.950 --> 08:56.050
You see, we're triplets.

08:57.800 --> 09:04.620
Well, we might as well tell you about our 
sleeping son before we tell you our wishes.

09:04.930 --> 09:08.930
Hulemy, I bet you know what this crystal is.

09:08.930 --> 09:11.920
Probably a crystal coffin?

09:11.920 --> 09:14.280
Correct as expected.

09:14.280 --> 09:15.700
What's that?

09:15.700 --> 09:19.550
They're magic items that 
were created long ago.

09:19.550 --> 09:25.170
I hear when someone enters one, their time 
stops indefinitely and they don't age.

09:25.580 --> 09:29.220
He has a negative blessing, as it turns out.

09:29.500 --> 09:30.960
Negative blessing?

09:31.360 --> 09:37.240
As you know, blessings are super 
powers one is granted by a good god.

09:37.240 --> 09:40.370
Lammis has the Blessing of Might, 
and I guess Boxxo has his barrier.

09:40.710 --> 09:46.600
And so, a negative blessing is a worthless 
power bestowed by an evil god.

09:46.850 --> 09:51.350
Thanks to that, he couldn't 
even manage everyday life.

09:51.620 --> 09:54.500
We couldn't bear to watch 
him get worse by the day,

09:54.500 --> 09:58.690
so we decided to have him stay asleep here 
until we could find a way to help him.

09:59.430 --> 10:03.790
<i>So, time has stood still for him 
and he's remained the same age.</i>

10:04.120 --> 10:07.850
Of the triplets, two of 
them had no problems,

10:07.850 --> 10:10.970
but he alone ended up with 
a negative blessing.

10:10.970 --> 10:12.750
As for what it is...

10:13.240 --> 10:14.540
It's the Blessing of Decay.

10:15.890 --> 10:21.360
An utterly horrid blessing, where not 
only does anything he touch rot,

10:21.360 --> 10:23.630
but his own body would 
gradually decay as well.

10:24.110 --> 10:29.140
To make matters worse, he was born 
with the Blessing of Hyper-Recovery.

10:30.140 --> 10:33.340
He feels the pain of his 
body continuously decaying,

10:33.340 --> 10:36.980
all while it regenerates 
due to Hyper-Recovery,

10:36.980 --> 10:40.210
and he must go on doing 
so until the day he dies.

10:40.650 --> 10:43.040
But why did he get a negative blessing?

10:43.250 --> 10:47.440
We once all but wiped out 
a certain team of hunters,

10:47.440 --> 10:53.040
and to get revenge they used an ancient 
cursed item to give him the negative blessing.

10:53.320 --> 11:00.540
Despite that, it took me a while to realize 
he'd been saddled with Blessing of Decay.

11:00.850 --> 11:05.840
By the time I figured it out, he could 
hardly even get around due to the pain.

11:06.350 --> 11:07.930
Great parenting, huh?

11:08.460 --> 11:13.560
<i>After hearing all this, even an idiot 
would know what their wish is.</i>

11:14.120 --> 11:18.380
Our wish is to get rid of 
his negative blessing.

11:18.380 --> 11:20.690
We're prepared to do anything for that.

11:21.130 --> 11:26.760
This crystal coffin's likely to be effective 
for another year to two at most, maybe less.

11:27.620 --> 11:29.370
We don't have much time.

11:29.700 --> 11:31.920
This is what we wanted to discuss.

11:32.350 --> 11:37.050
Would you defect with us over 
to the Netherlord's side?

11:37.960 --> 11:41.970
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

11:40.810 --> 11:41.970
<i>Boxxo.</i>

11:42.300 --> 11:44.960
Would you defect over to 
the Netherlord's side?

11:46.460 --> 11:48.050
Captain, that's messed up!

11:48.050 --> 11:50.390
He's the one who tried to kill us all!

11:50.390 --> 11:51.220
What a dumb—

11:50.600 --> 11:54.440
If I could exchange everyone's lives 
to do away with my son's pain,

11:54.440 --> 11:56.120
I'd gladly offer them up!

11:56.120 --> 11:58.980
Family is what's most important to me!

11:58.980 --> 12:03.470
Hey Captain, about this defection thing.

12:03.470 --> 12:05.370
How would you even do it?

12:05.370 --> 12:09.490
The commander who was on this stratum 
seems willing to arrange it.

12:09.490 --> 12:14.370
On the Netherlord's orders, she was planning 
on contacting us in the first place.

12:14.370 --> 12:15.990
That figures.

12:15.990 --> 12:19.700
We want to conquer the strata 
and get our wish granted.

12:19.700 --> 12:22.660
He wants us to get through 
to the final stratum,

12:22.660 --> 12:25.140
so he can take full control 
over the dungeon.

12:25.140 --> 12:26.880
Our interests happen to coincide.

12:26.880 --> 12:30.770
There's no guarantee the Netherlord 
would honor his side of the bargain.

12:30.770 --> 12:33.080
I'm aware of that.

12:33.080 --> 12:38.300
But look, how long would it take to defeat 
him and get the dungeon back to normal?

12:38.300 --> 12:41.160
We don't have time to do this the slow way!

12:41.160 --> 12:43.400
Even if we know it's a trap,

12:43.400 --> 12:45.660
it's the only thing we can cling to!

12:47.130 --> 12:51.980
Aren't there any of you who'd 
be willing to come with us?

12:51.980 --> 12:56.160
<i>We know the situation now, but our 
answer to that question is obvious.</i>

12:56.160 --> 12:58.180
So much for negotiation.

12:58.180 --> 12:59.550
That's too bad.

12:59.550 --> 13:02.300
<i>Y-ea, too bad.</i>

13:02.300 --> 13:05.360
You're the one we wanted the most, Boxxo.

13:05.360 --> 13:07.800
Boxxo will always stay with me!

13:07.800 --> 13:09.550
I'm not handing him over to anyone!

13:09.860 --> 13:14.470
Part of a clergyman's duty is to lead allies 
from folly back to a righteous path.

13:14.470 --> 13:18.310
Perhaps a poke from my weapon will 
bring you back to your senses.

13:18.310 --> 13:19.560
Or kill us.

13:19.560 --> 13:22.560
It's not like we're gonna 
go around killing anyone.

13:22.560 --> 13:26.190
We're just going to use the Netherlord 
so we can conquer the dungeon!

13:26.190 --> 13:29.060
He's probably thinking the same thing.

13:29.060 --> 13:31.690
He'll throw your group to the 
wolves once he's done with you.

13:31.690 --> 13:35.710
<i>Now what? Lammis doesn't have full 
control of her Blessing of Might.</i>

13:35.710 --> 13:38.730
<i>It's too dangerous for her to fight 
them under those conditions.</i>

13:38.730 --> 13:39.710
<i>I know!</i>

13:39.710 --> 13:42.960
<i>S-oo-i an-d S-i-s, co-m h-ea-r.</i>

13:46.090 --> 13:47.720
Thanks for the save, Boxxo.

13:47.720 --> 13:50.280
Wait a minute! Is "Sis" supposed to be me?!

13:50.280 --> 13:51.950
There's gotta be another option!

13:51.950 --> 13:53.600
<i>S-or-ry.</i>

13:53.920 --> 13:56.600
<i>I'll have to think of a 
more appropriate moniker.</i>

13:56.600 --> 13:59.850
Great, looks like there's 
no avoiding a fight.

14:00.150 --> 14:02.070
So let's do this, boys!

14:02.070 --> 14:03.480
You got it, Pops!

14:06.470 --> 14:08.950
Yeah, you're good at close combat, too!

14:08.950 --> 14:11.070
Only barely good enough, though.

14:11.490 --> 14:13.940
Hey, I'm here, too!

14:16.990 --> 14:18.730
Whoa, that's scary!

14:18.730 --> 14:20.240
One hit would be lethal!

14:20.240 --> 14:21.260
Don't worry, Aka.

14:21.260 --> 14:24.490
If you die, I'll go on dates with 
the girls you've tried to pick up.

14:24.490 --> 14:26.890
I didn't want to fight, but it's on!

14:28.220 --> 14:32.120
<i>I want to jump in too, but the room's 
so small, I'd hit my own people.</i>

14:32.500 --> 14:36.130
<i>I guess I'll just have to count on 
the efforts of Mishuel and Hevee.</i>

14:37.270 --> 14:40.210
Don't tell me you're slowing down, Hevee?

14:40.210 --> 14:42.520
I didn't expect your blades to be poisoned.

14:42.520 --> 14:44.830
The poison won't kill you.

14:44.830 --> 14:47.220
It'll just cause sharp pain all over...

14:48.150 --> 14:50.730
Hold on, does it not hurt?

14:50.730 --> 14:55.420
I used my blessing to 
temporarily relieve the pain.

14:55.420 --> 14:57.420
A blessing that relieves pain?

14:57.420 --> 15:01.350
Yes, the illusions and mind 
meddling are not magic.

15:01.350 --> 15:03.980
They're the power of the Blessing 
of Sensory Manipulation.

15:03.980 --> 15:06.910
I've never heard of a blessing like that.

15:06.910 --> 15:10.380
Hulemy, perhaps you have heard of it?

15:10.380 --> 15:14.770
Yeah. As blessings go, I hear it's 
about as rare as Boxxo's barrier.

15:14.770 --> 15:16.490
You're okay with me explaining it, Hevee?

15:16.490 --> 15:18.560
Sure, I do not mind.

15:18.560 --> 15:24.820
This blessing lets you control someone's 
senses, such as sight, hearing, smell, and taste.

15:24.820 --> 15:27.690
Looks like it can also control 
the sensation of pain.

15:27.690 --> 15:28.790
Wait a minute!

15:28.790 --> 15:31.320
Can it get rid of my son's pain?

15:31.320 --> 15:36.460
Unfortunately, I cannot use its 
analgesic effect on other people.

15:36.460 --> 15:38.090
Oh.

15:38.450 --> 15:41.190
I apologize for not meeting 
your expectations.

15:43.900 --> 15:46.050
This is such a pain.

15:44.940 --> 15:47.120
I wish you'd hold back more!

15:47.120 --> 15:49.260
You'd get away if I did.

15:49.260 --> 15:51.000
Filmina! Aka! Shiro!

15:51.000 --> 15:51.880
Right!

15:51.000 --> 15:51.880
Yeah!

15:51.000 --> 15:51.880
Okay!

15:51.880 --> 15:52.760
Here goes!

15:52.760 --> 15:55.140
<i>What? Are they about to try something?</i>

15:58.720 --> 15:59.960
<i>What's going on?!</i>

15:59.960 --> 16:01.890
<i>He was fine just a moment ago!</i>

16:01.890 --> 16:03.140
Hevee!

16:03.140 --> 16:05.270
<i>I don't know what he did to Hevee,</i>

16:05.270 --> 16:08.520
<i>but whatever they try,
I'll repel it all with my barrier!</i>

16:08.520 --> 16:12.250
Hevee's not the only one who's 
been hiding what he can do!

16:14.190 --> 16:16.320
<i>Wha? But I didn't turn it off!</i>

16:21.200 --> 16:25.050
<i>This is the spell Filmina used in 
battle against the crocodile fiends!</i>

16:25.050 --> 16:29.240
I never thought I'd have to use the secret 
weapon I was saving for the Netherlord.

16:32.150 --> 16:33.930
Master Boxxo! Everyone!

16:34.520 --> 16:36.300
I will give chase immediately!

16:35.670 --> 16:36.820
Don't do it.

16:36.820 --> 16:40.680
We don't know what the captain's power does, 
so chasing him alone is too dangerous!

16:41.410 --> 16:43.180
First let's see to Hevee!

16:43.480 --> 16:48.180
They really got us. I suppose he's 
not the captain for nothing.

16:48.810 --> 16:50.460
How can you be so calm?!

16:50.460 --> 16:52.940
Were you putting on an act 
so they could get away?!

16:52.940 --> 16:54.780
Perish the thought.

16:54.780 --> 16:57.780
I was immobilized by severe 
pain until a moment ago.

16:57.780 --> 17:02.330
Right now, I'm simply once again using 
my blessing to relieve the sensation.

17:02.330 --> 17:06.490
A blessing that can turn off Sensory
Manipulation, and also Boxxo's barrier...

17:06.490 --> 17:09.160
The captain's eyes were 
glowing red back there.

17:09.160 --> 17:11.670
I saw them, too. They were bright red.

17:11.670 --> 17:13.340
<i>Y-ea. Y-ea.</i>

17:13.340 --> 17:17.690
In that case, what comes to mind 
is the Blessing of Eye-Breach.

17:17.690 --> 17:21.090
It's practically a legend, and it 
lets you negate other blessings.

17:21.090 --> 17:24.570
<i>The captain's Blessing of Eye-Breach 
means serious trouble for me.</i>

17:24.570 --> 17:29.120
<i>If I can't use my barrier or Telekinesis, 
I'm nothing but a convenient vending machine.</i>

17:29.120 --> 17:33.040
<i>Oh, right. For a vending machine, 
I suppose that's fine.</i>

17:33.040 --> 17:35.870
We need to report this to the director.

17:35.870 --> 17:38.660
Shall we return to the village for now?

17:38.660 --> 17:40.530
Yeah, let's do that.

17:40.530 --> 17:43.920
They took off and left their son behind.

17:44.210 --> 17:47.750
They must think we won't harm him.

17:47.750 --> 17:50.300
He has done nothing wrong, after all.

17:56.210 --> 18:01.280
To get right to the point, I put Kerioyl 
and the others on the wanted list.

18:01.840 --> 18:04.440
To think they would betray us...

18:04.440 --> 18:06.850
It would seem I was "naïve."

18:06.850 --> 18:07.860
Sorry.

18:08.230 --> 18:12.530
I wish they had talked it over with 
us too, before making up their minds.

18:12.530 --> 18:15.880
The vice captain's circumstances 
probably had something to do with it.

18:15.880 --> 18:17.980
She isn't good at asking for help.

18:17.980 --> 18:20.380
I still wish they'd talked to us!

18:20.380 --> 18:22.450
Yes. Me, too.

18:23.100 --> 18:25.520
The way they left their precious son behind

18:25.520 --> 18:28.720
might be our fool captain's 
way of sending a message.

18:29.530 --> 18:31.630
<i>If only they hadn't felt 
backed into a corner...</i>

18:32.630 --> 18:35.650
<i>I should probably feel angry that 
they've done something so treacherous,</i>

18:35.650 --> 18:38.520
<i>but I just can't bring myself to.</i>

18:38.890 --> 18:42.520
Well, if we believe what Kerioyl said,

18:42.520 --> 18:46.630
they'll likely go to the final 
stratum and begin conquering it.

18:46.630 --> 18:50.770
How do you suppose they mean 
to travel between strata?

18:50.770 --> 18:52.610
Good question.

18:52.610 --> 18:57.000
The Netherlord might have some magic 
item for moving between strata.

18:57.000 --> 19:01.280
Or they could simply use the transfer 
circles that are deep within each stratum.

19:01.280 --> 19:04.310
<i>Oh right, there's a stratum lord 
in the depths of each stratum.</i>

19:04.310 --> 19:07.010
<i>A transfer circle appears if you defeat it.</i>

19:07.750 --> 19:12.410
However, I doubt we have to worry about 
them conquering the dungeon anytime soon.

19:12.410 --> 19:14.050
What do you mean?

19:14.050 --> 19:17.500
The four of them are not 
powerful enough alone.

19:17.500 --> 19:22.550
If they mean to outmaneuver the Netherlord, 
they'll need trustworthy comrades.

19:22.550 --> 19:27.310
Which means, they'll likely try to win 
someone over, or recruit acquaintances.

19:28.390 --> 19:30.180
The two remaining Menagerie members!

19:30.180 --> 19:32.550
Those two are oddballs.

19:32.550 --> 19:37.700
If the captain can cajole or bribe them, 
they could very well end up aiding him.

19:37.700 --> 19:40.580
Yeah, we can't rule that out.

19:40.580 --> 19:45.070
<i>If Hevee calls them oddballs, 
what exactly are they like?</i>

19:45.070 --> 19:49.590
Which means that while we're restoring 
the peace on each stratum,

19:49.590 --> 19:53.380
we should try to be the first to make 
contact with the remaining members,

19:53.380 --> 19:55.070
and win them over to our side.

19:55.070 --> 19:56.460
There you have it.

19:56.460 --> 19:59.650
But while the two of them should 
be somewhere inside the dungeon,

19:59.650 --> 20:02.630
I don't know which stratum they are on.

20:02.630 --> 20:08.100
It had been my responsibility to locate them,
but I was shut up inside the prison.

20:08.100 --> 20:12.080
<i>In the middle of an important mission, 
he was detained for acts of perversion.</i>

20:12.350 --> 20:15.620
In any case, we're in a bind right now.

20:15.620 --> 20:17.480
We can't freely travel between strata.

20:17.480 --> 20:20.660
Then let's go back to 
Clearflow Lake stratum.

20:20.660 --> 20:24.860
Restoration has only just begun. 
There's a long list of things to do.

20:25.120 --> 20:29.830
He's right. Let's all go back 
to Clearflow Lake stratum!

20:30.750 --> 20:33.490
<i>Too many different things 
happened on this stratum.</i>

20:34.180 --> 20:38.010
<i>And it's sure been a crazy 
time to be a vending machine.</i>

20:38.480 --> 20:42.920
<i>Here I am, doing something as important 
as crushing the Netherlord's ambitions.</i>

20:42.920 --> 20:46.180
<i>It would make sense if I were in 
the role of the legendary hero.</i>

20:46.180 --> 20:48.910
<i>But I'm a vending machine.</i>

20:49.540 --> 20:53.250
<i>Even so, my body might be inorganic, 
but my heart is human.</i>

20:53.250 --> 20:54.810
<i>I want to save everyone.</i>

20:54.810 --> 20:57.820
A lot's happened, but let's 
fight on together, Boxxo.

20:57.820 --> 20:59.240
<i>Hello there.</i>

20:59.570 --> 21:03.200
<i>Well, I don't know how much I can 
manage as a vending machine,</i>

21:03.200 --> 21:07.440
<i>but I'll devote all my electricity 
to keeping her and myself together!</i>

21:08.950 --> 21:11.210
All right, I'm activating it.

21:12.700 --> 21:14.070
Has it been tampered with?!

21:14.070 --> 21:14.950
Wh-What?!

21:14.950 --> 21:16.820
Everyone get away from the transfer circle!

21:16.820 --> 21:18.280
Except I can't move!

21:18.280 --> 21:21.250
Boxxo! Boxxo!

21:25.100 --> 21:26.310
<i>Where am I?</i>

21:27.760 --> 21:31.660
<i>Did I get sent to some 
other stratum by myself?</i>

21:31.660 --> 21:33.750
<i>Based on what Hulemy was shouting,</i>

21:33.750 --> 21:36.970
<i>something must have gone wrong 
with the transfer circle.</i>

21:36.970 --> 21:38.850
<i>I wonder if everyone's okay.</i>

21:38.850 --> 21:40.950
<i>And I'm concerned about Lammis.</i>

21:42.250 --> 21:45.640
<i>Oh, I'd better move, or I'll be in 
the way if someone else transfers.</i>

21:50.120 --> 21:52.640
<i>So, now what?</i>

21:52.640 --> 21:56.890
<i>Should I find a way to open the door 
and go out, or wait here instead?</i>

22:00.170 --> 22:02.170
<i>Hulemy! Director Bear!</i>

22:02.170 --> 22:03.040
<i>Lammis!</i>

22:03.040 --> 22:04.930
<i>Where's Lammis?!</i>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next Time</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>The Animals and the Girl</b>

23:34.980 --> 23:37.010
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:37.890 --> 23:40.020
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
